    <section class="cml-sensor-guide" id="cml-sensor-compatibility" aria-labelledby="cml-sensor-check-heading">
      <h2 id="cml-sensor-check-heading">Selection and interface compatibility checklist</h2>
      <p>Compare the offered model with the actual installation and acquisition input. A matching product name or connector shape does not establish electrical or mechanical interchangeability.</p>
      <p class="cml-note">On a small screen, scroll the comparison sideways to read all columns.</p>
      <div class="cml-sensor-table" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable sensor compatibility checklist" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Decision</th><th scope="col">Confirm before quotation</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach ($rows as [$label, $value]) echo '<tr><th scope="row">' . esc_html($label) . '</th><td>' . esc_html($value) . '</td></tr>'; ?></tbody></table></div>
      <?php if ($c['type'] === 'flow'): ?>
      <h3>Is this the same as a mud flow meter?</h3><p>Specify whether you need a relative flow indication, an absolute flow rate or accumulated volume. The paddle source record that lists a percentage explicitly says relative change, with no absolute range. It does not substantiate a calibrated drilling mud flow meter in absolute units. Ask for a model and installation-specific measurement definition before comparing offers.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'pump'): ?>
      <h3>What does a pump stroke sensor establish?</h3><p>The source records describe proximity sensing for pump/counting applications. Agree the target arrangement and receiving input before selecting a replacement. A stroke count alone does not establish measured fluid flow or delivered volume.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'density'): ?>
      <h3>Is mud density the same as shale density?</h3><p>No. Fluid density selection and shale sample density measurement have different objects and methods. State what is being measured before comparing instruments or calibration evidence.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'conductivity'): ?>
      <h3>Can I replace a conductivity probe without checking the transmitter?</h3><p>Confirm the probe, transmitter, compensation and receiving input together. The wireless source has conflicting output descriptions; require a configuration-matched wiring drawing before purchase.</p>
      <?php elseif (str_starts_with($c['type'], 'level_')): ?>
      <h3>Does a pit level sensor measure tank volume?</h3><p>The measurement path and reference determine distance or level. Volume requires a separate, verified relationship to tank geometry. Ultrasonic and radar records should be compared by installation and ordered interface, not treated as interchangeable.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'pressure'): ?>
      <h3>Can a standpipe pressure sensor replace a casing pressure sensor?</h3><p>Compare the actual measurement point, ordered range, process connection, sealing, medium and acquisition interface. The source records have different ranges and configurations; the application label alone does not prove equivalence. Resolve the MHP range conflict before using that record for pressure selection.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'torque'): ?>
      <h3>Does an electric torque sensor directly measure mechanical torque?</h3><p>These catalogue records describe electrical current sensing used in a torque-monitoring system. Current-to-torque indication requires a motor/drive-specific relationship and verification. Do not present a current measurement specification as independently established shaft-torque accuracy.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'depth'): ?>
      <h3>Does a depth encoder directly establish drilling depth?</h3><p>The source describes shaft rotation and two pulse channels. The logging system must interpret direction and scale movement using the actual rig arrangement and reference state. Request the resolution, counter settings and depth-calculation procedure; do not assume an absolute depth or precision from pulse output alone.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'hook'): ?>
      <h3>Is pressure range the same as hookload capacity?</h3><p>No. The hydraulic converter, rig arrangement and acquisition conversion determine hookload indication. Request the complete pressure-to-load calibration basis before comparing offers in load units.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'gas'): ?>
      <h3>Is a wireless H2S sensor a complete gas alarm system?</h3><p>A concentration-sensing node does not by itself establish the alarm, communication-failure response or personnel-protection arrangement. Request model-matched documentation and system verification; do not use catalogue response or life figures as complete-system guarantees.</p>
      <p>General background: <a href="https://www.osha.gov/hydrogen-sulfide/evaluating-controlling-exposure">OSHA — Hydrogen Sulfide: Evaluating and Controlling Exposure</a>. This is not a product manual, model approval or confirmation of compliance for the offered equipment or your site.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'wireless_master' || $c['type'] === 'wireless_system'): ?>
      <h3>Does the same radio frequency or a WITS label prove compatibility?</h3><p>No. Confirm paired devices, firmware, radio protocol, electrical interface and host data mapping. Verify data age, link-loss and recovery with the intended software. Regional documentation must match the offered configuration and destination.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'power'): ?>
      <h3>Can a battery or charger be replaced by matching voltage alone?</h3><p>No. Confirm pack chemistry, protection, connector/polarity, node fit and designated charger pairing. Obtain manufacturer instructions rather than combining catalogue charging statements into a new procedure.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'degasser'): ?>
      <h3>Can this meet a tubing degasser RFQ?</h3><p>The reviewed records describe gas collection and treatment in a mud logging sampling chain. If your tubing or process degassing RFQ has a different duty, provide fluid conditions, required throughput, pressure/vacuum requirements and acceptance criteria for engineering review. These records do not establish that duty or a guaranteed separation performance. Gas extraction equipment is not a gas analyser.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'fluoroscope'): ?>
      <h3>Does fluorescence colour directly establish oil content?</h3><p>The records describe visual observation and also mention mineral fluorescence and contamination. A colour description alone does not establish quantitative oil content or oil quality. If a quantitative result is required, request a separately validated method and appropriate instrument evidence.</p>
      <?php elseif ($c['type'] === 'display'): ?>
      <h3>Is the monitor an entire logging or gas-monitoring system?</h3><p>This record concerns a display/enclosure configuration. Confirm whether a host computer, application software, touch functions and cabling are included. The title and printed catalogue marking are not independent verification of certification for the exact supplied assembly.</p>
      <?php else: ?>
      <h3>Which temperature sensor details are still needed?</h3><p>The reviewed temperature records do not establish a complete model-specific electrical and mechanical configuration. Provide the existing nameplate or required measurement point, then confirm the sensing element/transmitter, range, output, probe geometry and acquisition input together.</p>
      <?php endif; ?>
      <h3 id="cml-sensor-documents">Technical documentation to obtain for the offered model</h3>
      <?php if ($c['slug'] === 'sitrans-probe-lu240-ultrasonic-pit-level-transmitter'): ?>
      <p data-cml-doc-status="official-family"><a href="https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/517/109973517/att_1294115/v45/A5E42673511en_LU240_HA_mA_OI_en-US.pdf">Siemens SITRANS Probe LU240 with mA/HART — Operating Instructions (PDF)</a>, 06/2024, A5E42673511-AH. Official manufacturer family reference for installation, connection, commissioning and technical data. Check the order code and firmware applicability. This is not a supplied-unit calibration record or approval certificate; request the order-matched documents below.</p>
      <?php else: ?>
      <p data-cml-doc-status="request-only">The material currently shown is an on-page catalogue record. This review has not verified a separate, model-matched manufacturer manual, wiring drawing or approval certificate; the list below is a request checklist, not a set of available downloads.</p>
      <?php endif; ?>
      <ul><?php foreach ($documents as $document) echo '<li>' . esc_html($document) . '</li>'; ?><li>Calibration/inspection records and acceptance criteria required for your order.</li><li>If a hazardous-area installation is required, the exact model and configuration, applicable approval documents and any barrier/interface requirements for technical review. Generic catalogue statements are not proof of approval.</li></ul>
      <div class="cml-actions"><?php echo cml_sensor_rfq($c, true); ?></div>
      <h3><?php echo in_array($c['type'], ['wireless_master', 'wireless_system', 'power', 'degasser', 'fluoroscope', 'display'], true) ? 'Prepare an equipment RFQ' : 'Prepare a sensor RFQ'; ?></h3><p>Include the existing model/nameplate, required measurement and units, supply and receiving interface, connector details, mounting dimensions, quantity, destination and target date. Mark unknown details so they can be reviewed. Our team will confirm the proposed configuration, documentation and commercial terms in the quotation.</p>
      <div class="cml-actions"><?php echo cml_sensor_rfq($c); ?></div>
      <h3>Related catalogue records and system scope</h3><ul><?php foreach ($related as $slug => $label) if ($slug !== $c['slug']) echo '<li>' . cml_sensor_link($slug, $label) . (in_array($c['type'], ['hook', 'gas', 'wireless_master', 'wireless_system', 'power', 'degasser', 'fluoroscope', 'display'], true) ? ' — confirm its role and compatibility in the complete configuration.</li>' : ' — compare documentation; not a confirmed equivalent.</li>'); ?></ul>
      <?php if (in_array($c['type'], ['degasser', 'fluoroscope', 'display'], true)): ?><p>Explore <a href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/product-category/formation-evaluation/')); ?>">formation evaluation equipment</a> and <a href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/product-category/drilling-monitoring/')); ?>">drilling monitoring equipment</a> to define the surrounding system and procurement scope.</p><?php endif; ?>
      <p>Review the <?php echo '<a href="' . esc_url(home_url('/product-category/mud-logging-sensors/')) . '">mud logging sensor catalogue</a>'; ?>, <?php echo '<a href="' . esc_url(home_url('/product-category/mud-logging-units/')) . '">complete logging unit and upgrade scope</a>'; ?> or <?php echo '<a href="' . esc_url(cml_page_url('products', 'en')) . '">equipment procurement guide</a>'; ?> to check the wider system boundary.</p>
    </section>
    <?php return (string)ob_get_clean();
}
add_filter('render_block_cml/product', function ($html) { $c = cml_sensor_context(); return $c ? $html . cml_sensor_quick($c) : $html; });
